findings.recommendation:
Record the convention change as refused on evidence. Build tools/os88live.py over a per-build -Le listing (kern_big, kern_small, kern_mega). It must model:
- fall-through entries;
- the kent/kret ladders;
- the OSAPI table;
- tail jumps.

Run it as a soak row that checks the 502 register-naming clobbers: headers and prints the dead-save list. Take the ~93 bytes inside the next size pass, not as a project.

findings.detail:
§18.95 already replaced the directory-only window (SPEC.md 39042-39048), so the caches are the sector cache and the FAT window. Map spans:
- kern_big: dsk_fatw_* 386 + dsk_bpb_sig 26 + dsk_fat_window 107 = 519 bytes of .cold.
- kern_small: 422.
- The sector cache: dsk_rah_* 513 .cold + 19 .text/.bss on kern_big.

A unified pool must add:
- per-slot dirty bits;
- a pin across dsk_next_clus_x's ES:BX read;
- a second pinned slot for the DX/DX+1 straddle, because chunks read forward to track end;
- a non-purgeable floor, because the FAT window may not be refused (18.8.3).

That is about +200 to +300. kern_small's FAT window is 2 sectors (1KB), against a 4.5KB track slot.

DRV_TITLES has no resident cost: pass 14 moved the titles into the blob and CTRL.DRV (driver.inc:1166-1172).

The resident cost is:
- 102 bytes of driver file names (map 0x939A-0x9406, less fdlg_s_drive);
- drv_tab, 11 rows x 16 = 176 bytes.

Name-keyed discovery removes:
- the names, -102;
- DRVR_FILE and DRVR_TITLE, -44;
- perhaps one row, -16.

It adds class-keyed lookups where code indexes a row (driver.inc:5642). drivers-10 (now, -~95) takes the same name bytes without a flag day.

The kernel-tree copies are:
- mega_a20/s/t (512 probes, FFFF:0510);
- mr_a20 (512);
- mega_wrprobe (a single test);
- kdp_a20w/t and kd_a20shut (512, alias FFFF:FFF0, because 0500 is kern_dos's own code on the HMA arm);
- kdh_tchk_src (65,536).

Two more were not counted: XMEM.DRV's xm_a20_* (XM_A20_SETTLE 512, XM_A20_ALIAS) and HDD.DRV's hd_xa_a20 (0510). mega.inc:10792 itself says its sequence is XMEM.DRV's.
